# Line-ending policy for this repository.
# Normalize text files to LF so the same physical files stay consistent across
# platforms. Without this, Windows clients (core.autocrlf=true) re-CRLF .md/.sh on
# checkout, breaking shell shebangs (#!/bin/bash) and producing phantom diffs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files need CRLF — cmd.exe mis-parses LF-terminated lines.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must stay LF: they run on Linux (cloud routine) where CRLF would break the
# shebang (#!/bin/bash). (Subsumed by the * rule above; kept explicit for intent.)
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts likewise need CRLF — LF-terminated try/catch blocks fail to parse.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
